#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43b9aafb-7456-5f41-8063-d0b78c7dd2fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{180}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518923} {:answer/id #uuid "48539ef9-0109-5101-b692-7f33dca51bb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "90\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518925} {:answer/id #uuid "57aafb72-bdac-55be-80f7-7b85776228a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "180\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518932} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa80141-2ce2-5349-94f1-543788e1555c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "32400\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518941} {:answer/id #uuid "ea8be9f3-91f4-5cba-858d-41aaac0aa322" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "360\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518968}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518932} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a1f8f25-3418-59b0-ba6b-72dab84b9c04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4bedfcff-a678-5213-96c3-9e61ef2500d0" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}\\\\\\left(u - v\\right)^{3}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}4 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)&8 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)\\\\3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2}&- 3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(4 \\left(u + 2 v\\right))\\cdot (- 3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2})-(8 \\left(u + 2 v\\right))\\cdot (3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2})\\\\& =- 36 u^{3} + 108 u v^{2} - 72 v^{3}\\\\& =- 36 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2} \\left(u + 2 v\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(1,2)} & =\\left(- 36 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2} \\left(u + 2 v\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=1,v=2}\\\\& =- 36 \\left((1) - (2)\\right)^{2} \\left((1) + 2 (2)\\right)\\\\& =-180\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-180|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =180\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518930 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26961c66-edcd-5145-85c4-6c1fc54d0f34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3600\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518913} {:answer/id #uuid "6037566d-f7b6-50da-a88b-dfbdeeb3fcc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "60\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518935} {:answer/id #uuid "76383b00-80af-5d97-ab38-8ebc7d2e3bb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{60}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518940} {:answer/id #uuid "812363c8-d6ee-5aea-85f6-8c6219b20949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "120\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518943} {:answer/id #uuid "ec0f0246-49a2-593f-b299-8edb618ae39c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "30\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518969}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518935} :answer-field/id #uuid "d336bb06-ff1c-5772-90e6-a62e20ceb52d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518962}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "53cbe52b-bde0-5c41-aca4-4e6c21faa397" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(2,-1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}3 u v^{3}\\\\u^{2} + 2 v^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}3 v^{3}&9 u v^{2}\\\\2 u&4 v\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(3 v^{3})\\cdot (4 v)-(9 u v^{2})\\cdot (2 u)\\\\& =- 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 12 v^{4}\\\\& =- 6 v^{2} \\left(3 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(2,-1)} & =\\left(- 6 v^{2} \\left(3 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=2,v=-1}\\\\& =- 6 (-1)^{2} \\left(- 2 (-1)^{2} + 3 (2)^{2}\\right)\\\\& =-60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-60|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =60\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518944 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18d61485-2e83-5936-bf4f-bdb56bc3c4ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "972\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518910} {:answer/id #uuid "1c320d3a-60da-5b71-a776-74db91358bd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{486}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518911} {:answer/id #uuid "45580a5e-5bf5-591a-975f-b5c6caffce26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "243\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518924} {:answer/id #uuid "981bec3c-d327-540d-b022-7683af7469d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "486\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518949} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f24ccd-920b-5556-ac5f-da611e02a4e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "236196\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518959}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518949} :answer-field/id #uuid "f515b64d-d940-5cd5-9894-9abe522a7fe6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518973}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "829d2336-b2c1-5d22-81da-62efc70bcbb3" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-1,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}\\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{3}\\\\\\left(u - v\\right)^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}3 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}&6 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}\\\\2 \\left(u - v\\right)&- 2 \\left(u - v\\right)\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(3 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2})\\cdot (- 2 \\left(u - v\\right))-(6 \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2})\\cdot (2 \\left(u - v\\right))\\\\& =- 18 u^{3} - 54 u^{2} v + 72 v^{3}\\\\& =- 18 \\left(u - v\\right) \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-1,2)} & =\\left(- 18 \\left(u - v\\right) \\left(u + 2 v\\right)^{2}\\right)\\big|_{u=-1,v=2}\\\\& =- 18 \\left((-1) - (2)\\right) \\left((-1) + 2 (2)\\right)^{2}\\\\& =486\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|486|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =486\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518946 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09aa9167-b044-5501-8f63-4ce19c39ae5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "180\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518905} {:answer/id #uuid "09d9affe-0d42-57ca-8777-3fbb4b43fa8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "360\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518906} {:answer/id #uuid "979d8129-4d6e-5b64-adf3-cad4bb9f306b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "32400\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518948} {:answer/id #uuid "c371dc56-8562-5f1d-88cd-cbe72dc4bff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "90\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518961} {:answer/id #uuid "d50691b4-